      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if we could delay starting the table until we knew that we were actually running enough things to use it? In the no-op case, or when we\u0027re only compiling a few quick items, I can\u0027t even visually see the table, but it still uses up more vertical scrolling space in my terminal.\n\nMaybe use one of the lines to show the currently running execution count? (bazel uses the progress line when there\u0027s more than one thing running to provide that count, and never shows a completed action description)\n\nSomewhat separately, I was wondering if we shouldn\u0027t even add things to the table until they\u0027ve hit 1(2?) second of runtime, just to limit churn on short actions. The progress/finished line can show that something is quickly happening.",
